steps.text:
[Traditional periodisation](g:traditional-periodisation) starts the macrocycle with lots of easy volume and slowly trades it for less volume and more intensity as the main race nears. Many abilities (aerobic base, threshold, strength, speed) are trained side by side, "mixed", all year.

Issurin, a leading advocate of the block model, lists its weak points [[c:per-trad-limits]]:

- mixed training sends competing signals;
- long periods of many-targeted training pile up fatigue;
- each ability gets only a diluted dose;
- it is built for one peak, so it copes badly with several important races in a season.

These are arguments from a review, not trial results.
